## 9. Hydra vs. John the Ripper vs. Hashcat

These tools address different password-testing workflows.

| Tool | Primary purpose | Typical input |
|---|---|---|
| Hydra | Online authentication testing | Live network service |
| John the Ripper | Password-hash auditing and recovery | Password hash file |
| Hashcat | Password-hash auditing and recovery | Password hash file |

### Online vs. Offline Testing

**Online authentication testing** sends authentication attempts to a live service. Defensive controls such as rate limiting and account lockouts may affect the results.

**Offline password-hash recovery** compares candidate passwords against stored password hashes without repeatedly authenticating to the original service.

Offline recovery depends on the hash algorithm, password strength, candidate-generation strategy, and available computing resources.

**Key distinction:** Hydra tests live authentication services; John the Ripper and Hashcat commonly perform offline password-hash recovery.

